OLD_SECTION (line 42)
- **Both overlay background modes** [em dash] `color` tints the overlay, `blur` blurs `#page` behind it instead. Switch with the dropdown; it applies from the next open, since config is snapshotted per layer. Note the blur is held while any layer wants it and only lifts when the stack empties.
- **Stacking** [em dash] Sign in → Forgot password → Terms is three layers deep. `Escape` pops one layer at a time, in reverse order. The live **Open layers** counter tracks `depth`.
- **One stack across instances** [em dash] "Help" is opened by a second `ModalDisplayer` with its own trigger class and effect, yet it layers correctly on the profile modal and one `Escape` still pops exactly one layer.
- **`closeAll()`** from a button *inside* a modal. It is placed there deliberately: a page-level button cannot dismiss a stack, because the overlay blocks the page [em dash] which is the whole point of a modal.
NEW_SECTION (line 42)
- **Both overlay background modes**: `color` tints the overlay, `blur` blurs `#page` behind it instead. Switch with the dropdown; it applies from the next open, since config is snapshotted per layer. Note the blur is held while any layer wants it and only lifts when the stack empties.
- **Stacking**: Sign in → Forgot password → Terms is three layers deep. `Escape` pops one layer at a time, in reverse order. The live **Open layers** counter tracks `depth`.
- **One stack across instances**: "Help" is opened by a second `ModalDisplayer` with its own trigger class and effect, yet it layers correctly on the profile modal and one `Escape` still pops exactly one layer.
- **`closeAll()`** from a button *inside* a modal. It is placed there deliberately: a page-level button cannot dismiss a stack, because the overlay blocks the page, which is the whole point of a modal.
REASON
Em dash cleanup (workspace rule: no em dashes in any project). Each U+2014 is rewritten by context: a colon for an explanation or list, a comma before a conjunction (and, but, which...) or when the clause already has a colon, parentheses for a paired aside, a hyphen for an empty value (table cells, placeholders). Sentences the first pass garbled were corrected by hand after two features-validator reviews. No wording or behaviour change otherwise.

